%T A399002 14651,26955,52441,96302,185782,353835,684607,1287849,2534791,4798045,
%U A399002 9245219,18053507,34704774,66315065,131070763,249667893,488309683,956813471,1859096835,3588419090,7092581077
%N A399002 Sum of the fixed-content bracelet counts over the distinct multiplicity-collapse profiles of the integer partitions of n.
%C A399002 For a partition lambda of n, let c(lambda) be the partition obtained by listing, in weakly decreasing order, the multiplicities of the distinct part sizes of lambda. Let C(n) = {c(lambda): lambda is a partition of n}; repeated collapse profiles are included only once.
%C A399002 For a partition Q, let G(Q) be the number of fixed-content bracelets with color-multiplicity profile Q; that is, the number of dihedral orbits of words with content Q. Then a(n) is the sum of G(Q) over the distinct Q in C(n).
%C A399002 The collapse forgets the numerical sizes of the parts of lambda but retains how often each distinct size occurs. For example, c((4,4,2,1,1,1))=(3,2,1).
%C A399002 The companion sequence A396575 replaces dihedral orbits by cyclic orbits. Every term satisfies A396575(n) >= a(n).
%H A399002 Andrea Cutri, <a href="https://github.com/aku-79/oeis-refined-atlas/blob/main/programs/a399002.py">Python program</a>.
%F A399002 a(n) = Sum_{q in C(n)} G(q), where C(n) = {c(lambda): lambda is a partition of n} and each distinct q is included once. For q=(q_1,...,q_k) with m=Sum_i q_i, let M(q) = (1/m) * Sum_{d | gcd(q_1,...,q_k)} phi(d) * (m/d)! / Product_i (q_i/d)!, and let [x^q] denote the coefficient of x_1^{q_1}...x_k^{q_k}. Define H(q) = [x^q] (x_1+...+x_k)(x_1^2+...+x_k^2)^((m-1)/2) if m is odd, and H(q) = (1/2) * [x^q] ((x_1^2+...+x_k^2)^(m/2) + (x_1+...+x_k)^2 (x_1^2+...+x_k^2)^((m-2)/2)) if m is even. Then G(q) = (M(q) + H(q))/2.
%e A399002 C(4) = {(1), (1,1), (2), (2,1), (4)}. Each of these five profiles has one bracelet, so a(4)=5.
%e A399002 For n=6 the ten collapse profiles are (1), (1,1), (2), (1,1,1), (2,1), (3), (2,2), (3,1), (4,1), and (6). Their bracelet counts are respectively 1,1,1,1,1,1,2,1,1,1, giving a(6)=11. The only difference from the cyclic companion at n=6 occurs for Q=(1,1,1), where the two chiral necklaces form one bracelet.
%Y A399002 Cf. A005651, A072605, A213943. Companion sequence: A396575.
